{"type":"message","id":"e83c6c40","parentId":"82ac7bd4","timestamp":"2026-03-26T17:28:59.215Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] Got it — then I’d treat it as *your* repo/project, not just a fork to side-eye.\n\nMy honest take from the page alone:\n- It presents well.\n- The architecture sounds coherent enough for an LLM research/trading framework.\n- The strongest parts of the pitch are:\n  - clear agent-role decomposition\n  - CLI + Web UI\n  - multi-provider model support\n  - concrete data-provider story\n  - a specific strategy angle instead of generic “AI trading”\n\nWhere I’d still be tough on it:\n- The README makes big promises, so anyone disputing it will go after:\n  - whether features are fully implemented vs partially scaffolded\n  - whether the Web UI is robust or mostly demo-grade\n  - whether “JadeCap ICT” is genuinely encoded in logic/prompts or mostly branding\n  - whether performance implications are overstated\n\nIf you want help defending it, I can do that properly — not fluff, actual evidence.\n\nI can:\n1. audit your codebase and extract proof points,\n2. compare your repo against upstream to show your original work,\n3. build a dispute-ready summary:\n   - what you changed\n   - what is genuinely implemented\n   - what claims are supportable\n   - where wording should be tightened to avoid attacks\n\nIf you want, send me the dispute angle:\n- “they say it’s copied”\n- “they say it doesn’t work”\n- “they say features are fake”\n- “they refunded / chargeback / platform complaint”\n\nThen I’ll tailor the review for that exact fight.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0683a763bd3bba040169c56cd056ac819b8563be641d690c82\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":260,"output":332,"cacheRead":18048,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":18640,"cost":{"input":0.0006500000000000001,"output":0.00498,"cacheRead":0.0045119999999999995,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.010142}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774546125940,"responseId":"resp_0683a763bd3bba040169c56ccf6500819b8e9a2486c8f6eedf"}}
{"type":"message","id":"50390522","parentId":"e83c6c40","timestamp":"2026-03-26T17:29:24.435Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"openclaw-control-ui\",\n  \"id\": \"openclaw-control-ui\"\n}\n```\n\n[Thu 2026-03-26 12:29 CDT] Now i want it plug in openclaw for you to use it is that possible"}],"timestamp":1774546164433}}
{"type":"message","id":"bb17f42e","parentId":"50390522","timestamp":"2026-03-26T17:29:47.289Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] Yes, probably — but it depends on what you mean by “plug into OpenClaw.”\n\nThere are 3 realistic levels:\n\n1. **Run it locally and I help operate it**\n- Easiest path\n- You install/start TradingAgents in the workspace or elsewhere\n- I can read/edit configs, run commands, inspect logs, and use its outputs\n- Best if you want me to help use/debug it quickly\n\n2. **Wrap it as an OpenClaw skill**\n- Good if you want a repeatable workflow\n- I’d create a skill that documents:\n  - how to launch it\n  - how to pass ticker/date/provider inputs\n  - how to read results\n  - how to use CLI vs Web UI\n- This makes it much easier for future me to use reliably\n\n3. **Expose it as a tool/service OpenClaw can call**\n- Most powerful, more work\n- Usually done by:\n  - adding a local CLI wrapper, or\n  - exposing an HTTP/MCP-style interface, then\n  - connecting that into OpenClaw workflows\n- Best if you want “ask OpenClaw to analyze NVDA” and have it call your system directly\n\nMy recommendation:\n- **First do level 1**\n- Then **level 2**\n- Only do level 3 if you want real automation\n\nA few concrete integration options:\n\n### Option A — CLI integration\nIf your project already has a working command like:\n- `tradingagents`\n- or `python -m cli.main`\n\nthen I can drive it through shell commands and file outputs.\n\n### Option B — Web UI integration\nIf `python run_webui.py` starts a local app, I can use the browser tool to interact with it on `localhost:8000`.\n\n### Option C — API wrapper\nIf there’s a Python entrypoint like `TradingAgentsGraph(...).propagate(...)`, I can help build:\n- a tiny script\n- or a local HTTP API\nso OpenClaw can invoke it cleanly.\n\n### Best long-term OpenClaw-native shape\nI’d suggest one of these:\n- **Skill**: “Use TradingAgents for market analysis”\n- **MCP/local service**: structured calls like:\n  - analyze ticker\n  - fetch run history\n  - export report\n  - inspect memories\n\nIf you want, I can set this up with you.\n\nThe fastest next step is:\n1. clone or point me at the repo locally\n2. I inspect its entrypoints\n3. I tell you the cleanest OpenClaw integration path\n4. I can build the wrapper/skill\n\nIf you want me to proceed, send one of:\n- “clone it and inspect”\n- “it’s already at /path/to/repo”\n- “make it an OpenClaw skill”\n- “make a local API wrapper for it”","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0683a763bd3bba040169c56cf8a748819ba8ce754fb98148a1\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":153,"output":600,"cacheRead":18560,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":19313,"cost":{"input":0.00038250000000000003,"output":0.009000000000000001,"cacheRead":0.00464,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.014022500000000002}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774546164435,"responseId":"resp_0683a763bd3bba040169c56cf68d98819b98f7e1431d21bc91"}}
{"type":"message","id":"bce6e7f1","parentId":"bb17f42e","timestamp":"2026-03-26T17:31:52.538Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"openclaw-control-ui\",\n  \"id\": \"openclaw-control-ui\"\n}\n```\n\n[Thu 2026-03-26 12:31 CDT] Expose it as a tool/service OpenClaw can call"}],"timestamp":1774546312536}}
{"type":"message","id":"6b3e09df","parentId":"bce6e7f1","timestamp":"2026-03-26T17:31:56.707Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_6T1MqfYKavoCZF2wRoLRexre|fc_0683a763bd3bba040169c56d8d170c819b9b737f388b4aa9b7","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"~/openclaw/skills/mcporter/SKILL.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"~/openclaw/skills/mcporter/SKILL.md\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":181,"output":30,"cacheRead":19200,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":19411,"cost":{"input":0.00045250000000000005,"output":0.00045,"cacheRead":0.0048,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.005702499999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774546312539,"responseId":"resp_0683a763bd3bba040169c56d8961b0819b9fc866f93e667975"}}
{"type":"message","id":"61f47954","parentId":"6b3e09df","timestamp":"2026-03-26T17:31:56.713Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_6T1MqfYKavoCZF2wRoLRexre|fc_0683a763bd3bba040169c56d8d170c819b9b737f388b4aa9b7","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: mcporter\ndescription: Use the mcporter CLI to list, configure, auth, and call MCP servers/tools directly (HTTP or stdio), including ad-hoc servers, config edits, and CLI/type generation.\nhomepage: http://mcporter.dev\nmetadata:\n  {\n    \"openclaw\":\n      {\n        \"emoji\": \"📦\",\n        \"requires\": { \"bins\": [\"mcporter\"] },\n        \"install\":\n          [\n            {\n              \"id\": \"node\",\n              \"kind\": \"node\",\n              \"package\": \"mcporter\",\n              \"bins\": [\"mcporter\"],\n              \"label\": \"Install mcporter (node)\",\n            },\n          ],\n      },\n  }\n---\n\n# mcporter\n\nUse `mcporter` to work with MCP servers directly.\n\nQuick start\n\n- `mcporter list`\n- `mcporter list <server> --schema`\n- `mcporter call <server.tool> key=value`\n\nCall tools\n\n- Selector: `mcporter call linear.list_issues team=ENG limit:5`\n- Function syntax: `mcporter call \"linear.create_issue(title: \\\"Bug\\\")\"`\n- Full URL: `mcporter call https://api.example.com/mcp.fetch url:https://example.com`\n- Stdio: `mcporter call --stdio \"bun run ./server.ts\" scrape url=https://example.com`\n- JSON payload: `mcporter call <server.tool> --args '{\"limit\":5}'`\n\nAuth + config\n\n- OAuth: `mcporter auth <server | url> [--reset]`\n- Config: `mcporter config list|get|add|remove|import|login|logout`\n\nDaemon\n\n- `mcporter daemon start|status|stop|restart`\n\nCodegen\n\n- CLI: `mcporter generate-cli --server <name>` or `--command <url>`\n- Inspect: `mcporter inspect-cli <path> [--json]`\n- TS: `mcporter emit-ts <server> --mode client|types`\n\nNotes\n\n- Config default: `./config/mcporter.json` (override with `--config`).\n- Prefer `--output json` for machine-readable results.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1774546316712}}
